***FOOTNOTES***

     [1]  MSHA categorizes electrical voltage as follows:

     low-voltage ranges from 1 to 660; medium-voltage ranges
     from 661 to 1,000; and high-voltage is anything over
     1,000 (Tr. 29).

     [2]  MSHA electrical qualification cards issued under
     section 77.103 are as follows:

      underground low/medium-voltage is orange; surface
      low/medium-voltage is green; and underground/surface
      high-voltage is white (Tr. 426-427, 434-435).



